{
  "title": "SystemMethods",
  "description": "The five scheduler phases a System may participate in, one per dispatch stage of the Application frame loop: pre-simulation sync, fixed-timestep simulation, variable-rate update, rendering, and post-flush work. Every phase must be synchronous. The registry dispatches them on the frame path and never awaits a result, so an `async` phase is a compile error (see Synchronous) and, for callers the type system cannot reach, a thrown error in every build. Asynchronous work belongs in the owning scene's Scene.load.",
